§§ `Order s 17 — commencement; s 16 — repeal of the 1980 Order`

-- src:72 | סעיף 16 – ביטול
-- src:73 | צו מס הכנסה (כללים לעיגול סכומים), התשמ״א–1980 – בטל.
-- src:75 | סעיף 17 – תחילה
-- src:76 | תחילתו של צו זה ביום כ׳ בטבת התשמ״ו (1 בינואר 1986).
@ref Rounding Order ss 16-17 (source lines 72-76)
GIVEN `the day the adjustment is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Order s 17 — the Order is in force on` `the day the adjustment is made` MEANS
    `the day the adjustment is made` AT LEAST YMD 1986 1 1

-- The Order was not itself repealed in the deposited text, which is the Ordinance as amended at
-- retrieval and the Order as consolidated in 2025. Whether anything replaced it since is a fact
-- the deposited sources do not show. (NOTES.md, assumption A2.)

§§ `The rule of every section of the Order: the round amount and the excess over it`

-- (a): the round amount is the multiple of N that does not exceed the adjusted amount.
@ref Rounding Order s 1(a)-(b), the same in ss 2, 4-8 and 10-13 (source lines 15-16 and the like)
GIVEN `the adjusted amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the step`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the round amount of` `the adjusted amount` `in steps of` `the step` MEANS
    `the step` TIMES FLOOR (`the adjusted amount` DIVIDED BY `the step`)

-- The refusal for an amount below nought: an adjusted amount is a sum of money, and the Order
-- says nothing of a negative one.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Order rounds an adjusted amount, and nought is the least one it speaks of` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Rounding Order rounds adjusted amounts, and says nothing of a negative one"

-- (b): the excess is "not taken into account" below half a step, and a step is added from half a step.
@ref Rounding Order s 1(b), the same in ss 2, 4-8 and 10-13
GIVEN `the adjusted amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the step`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Order rounds` `the adjusted amount` `in steps of` `the step` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the adjusted amount` LESS THAN 0 THEN `the Order rounds an adjusted amount, and nought is the least one it speaks of`
        IF `the excess` LESS THAN `the step` DIVIDED BY 2 THEN `the round amount`
        OTHERWISE `the round amount` PLUS `the step`
    WHERE
        `the round amount` MEANS `the round amount of` `the adjusted amount` `in steps of` `the step`
        `the excess`       MEANS `the adjusted amount` MINUS `the round amount`

