§§ `Which section of the Order rounds which kind of amount`

-- Section 120B(a) names five groups of amount. The Order has a rule for the first three kinds
-- outright and for ten of the amounts in the fourth group (the "social deductions" of s 120A),
-- and none for the rest of the fourth group nor for the fifth (recognised donation amounts,
-- s 46(a)). For those, section 120B(d) says only that the Minister "may" make rounding rules.
-- That is fork R1: the text does not say what an amount is when the Minister has made no rule.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 120B(d) (source line 4341-4342 in the Ordinance file); fork R1; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for`
`rounding — the reading this row takes for an amount the Order has no rule for` MEANS
    `the rounding of such an amount is declined`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to"

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 120B(d); fork R1
GIVEN `the adjusted amount` IS A NUMBER
      r                     IS A `A reading of an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for` `the adjusted amount` `, reading it as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the rounding of such an amount is declined` THEN `the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to`
    WHEN `such an amount stays as adjusted`           THEN `the adjusted amount`

@ref Rounding Order ss 1-13; Income Tax Ordinance s 120A "social deductions", s 120B(a), (d); fork R1
GIVEN `the adjusted amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the kind`            IS AN `An amount that section 120B adjusts, or that the Rounding Order rounds`
      r                     IS A `A reading of an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Order rounds the adjusted amount` `the adjusted amount` `as an amount of the kind` `the kind` `, reading an amount it has no rule for as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `an income ceiling`                                                    THEN `Order s 1 — round an income ceiling` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `the amount of a credit point`                                         THEN `Order s 2 — round the amount of credit points` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `the amount of an allowance point`                                     THEN `Order s 3 — round the amount of allowance points` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `the exemption of a blind or 100% disabled person, section 9(5)(a)`    THEN `Order s 4 — round the exemption of section 9(5)(a)` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `the exemption of a blind or disabled person not from personal exertion, section 9(5)(b)` THEN `Order s 5 — round the exemption of section 9(5)(b)` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `a retirement grant or death grant, sections 9(7A) and 32(9)(a)(1)`    THEN `Order s 6 — round a retirement grant or a death grant` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `the discount an employee receives from the employer, section 9(20)`   THEN `Order s 7 — round the discounts an employee receives` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `a qualifying annuity, section 9A(a) and (c)`                          THEN `Order s 8 — round a qualifying annuity` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `the exempt amount, section 9A(b)`                                     THEN `Order s 9 — round the exempt amount` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `the ceiling for medical-expenses credit, section 44(a)(1)`            THEN `Order s 10 — round the ceiling for medical expenses` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `the amount for credit, section 45A(d)`                                THEN `Order s 11 — round the amount for credit` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `qualifying income, section 47`                                        THEN `Order s 12 — round qualifying income` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `a fine for failing to file a report, section 188`                     THEN `Order s 13 — round the fine` `the adjusted amount`
    WHEN `an amount in section 9(16A), (16B) or (18A)`                          THEN `an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for` `the adjusted amount` `, reading it as` r
    WHEN `the amount in section 17(5A)`                                         THEN `an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for` `the adjusted amount` `, reading it as` r
    WHEN `an amount in section 32(9) other than the grant of paragraph (a)(1)`  THEN `an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for` `the adjusted amount` `, reading it as` r
    WHEN `an amount in section 45A other than subsection (d)`                   THEN `an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for` `the adjusted amount` `, reading it as` r
    WHEN `the amount in section 58A(c)`                                         THEN `an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for` `the adjusted amount` `, reading it as` r
    WHEN `an amount in section 125D`                                            THEN `an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for` `the adjusted amount` `, reading it as` r
    WHEN `a recognised donation amount, section 46(a)`                          THEN `an amount the Rounding Order has no rule for` `the adjusted amount` `, reading it as` r

-- The same, at the reading this row takes (the default: declined).
GIVEN `the adjusted amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the kind`            IS AN `An amount that section 120B adjusts, or that the Rounding Order rounds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Order rounds the adjusted amount` `the adjusted amount` `as an amount of the kind` `the kind` MEANS
    `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` `the adjusted amount` `as an amount of the kind` `the kind`
        `, reading an amount it has no rule for as` `rounding — the reading this row takes for an amount the Order has no rule for`

§§ `The alternative readings of limb (a), for the tests only`

-- "Nearest", with a tie going to the lower multiple, and then limb (b) applied to the excess over that.
@ref Rounding Order s 1(a)-(b); the argument in the header of this module
GIVEN `the adjusted amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the step`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going down, then (b):` `the adjusted amount` `in steps of` `the step` MEANS
    IF   `the excess over the nearest` LESS THAN `the step` DIVIDED BY 2
    THEN `the nearest`
    ELSE `the nearest` PLUS `the step`
    WHERE
        `the floor`   MEANS `the round amount of` `the adjusted amount` `in steps of` `the step`
        `the nearest` MEANS IF   (`the adjusted amount` MINUS `the floor`) AT MOST `the step` DIVIDED BY 2
                            THEN `the floor`
                            ELSE `the floor` PLUS `the step`
        `the excess over the nearest` MEANS `the adjusted amount` MINUS `the nearest`

-- "Nearest", with a tie going to the higher multiple, and then limb (b).
@ref Rounding Order s 1(a)-(b); the argument in the header of this module
GIVEN `the adjusted amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the step`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going up, then (b):` `the adjusted amount` `in steps of` `the step` MEANS
    IF   `the excess over the nearest` LESS THAN `the step` DIVIDED BY 2
    THEN `the nearest`
    ELSE `the nearest` PLUS `the step`
    WHERE
        `the floor`   MEANS `the round amount of` `the adjusted amount` `in steps of` `the step`
        `the nearest` MEANS IF   (`the adjusted amount` MINUS `the floor`) LESS THAN `the step` DIVIDED BY 2
                            THEN `the floor`
                            ELSE `the floor` PLUS `the step`
        `the excess over the nearest` MEANS `the adjusted amount` MINUS `the nearest`
